==Enemy==
Spacefish Jones is more glass cannon-oriented than Sunfish Jones, dealing up to 19,744 damage when first encountered and almost 30,000 in its strongest appearances. It also sports a [[Barrier]] with 12,000 HP, meaning it can survive longer against your weaker cats, plus a faster movement speed allowing it to advance easier.

==Strategy==
Spacefish Jones is considerably less durable than [[Sunfish Jones]], not to mention its two traits are pretty easy to exploit with a clear shot. Despite its Barrier strength, it is still relatively weak and may not necessarily require a dedicated Barrier Breaker. The obvious strategy would be to use fast melee units like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], [[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]] and [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman]] to exploit its long attack delay and in the latter case, its Floating trait. However, you'll have to time them properly to get the most out of them, and make sure no other threats can get in the way. If you can accumulate enough DPS, Spacefish Jones won't be able to fire off enough attacks, either, as it has three knockbacks, and so even in its strongest appearances there may be a chance to regain ground against it. Just remember to replace destroyed units quickly before it pushes.

Slower melee units like [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]] or [[Crazed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed M. Titan Cat]] can tank multiple hits from Spacefish Jones, and the former can help to interrupt its attack animation. At high levels, [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cat]] can also be a serviceable counter, but his single target hinders him greatly.

In terms of ranged units, only a few work well, as Spacefish Jones's range is so high that it will end up hitting them anyways and many of them lack the necessary defensive attributes, making it near-impossible to snipe. However, means to hit behind the frontline, especially waves and surges, do remain valuable if they are long enough to reach Spacefish Jones, such as in the case of [[Gravi (Uber Rare Cat)|Gravolodon]], whose resistance to Aliens, Barrier Breaker and Waves enable it to easily snipe Jones. Additionally, Spacefish Jones is often seen supporting melee pushers, so units that can deal with them are still valuable to bring.

