==Trivia==
*Spacefish Jones's Japanese name, Space Manborg (スペースマンボルグ ''Supēsumanborugu''), is derived from 翻車魚 ''manbō'' (sunfish) and possibly the game ''[[wikia:gradius:Space Manbow|Space Manbow]]'' (スペースマンボウ ''Supēsumanbō'').
**Although the Japanese names of [[Sunfish Jones]], Spacefish Jones and [[Jumbo Jones]] all have parts that can be taken as "borg", they aren't all the same: Sunfish Jones and Jumbo Jones have ボーグ ''bōgu'', while Spacefish Jones has ボルグ ''borugu''.
*Spacefish Jones may be based on the [[wikipedia:Atlantic spadefish|spadefish]], as both Spacefish Jones and Sunfish Jones are very compressed and disk-shaped, hence the claim that Spacefish Jones is "invisible" when viewed at the front. In fact, 'Spacefish' and 'Spadefish' are only a single letter apart.
*Its description may be a vague reference to the Northrop Grumman [[wikipedia:Northrop Grumman B-2 Spirit|B-2 Spirit]] stealth bomber, as it is mentioned in Sunfish Jones' entry, and Spacefish Jones also has a stealth-relevant design.
*Both its English and Japanese descriptions break the 4th wall, as they mention it being present in a game.

